    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_42f9fbae44e1a2a83459e9ec192aa4be622634937b43995960fffc23222bb335",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The original eta coordinates connect local Laurent data to the nontrivial-zero power sums plus an explicit zeta tail, whereas subtracting six known trivial-zero poles moves those singular contributions into explicit correction terms and leaves residual coefficients with a convergence radius enlarged to thirteen. This analytic preconditioning improves the residual coefficient scale but sacrifices the original arithmetic interpretation and does not itself control the new binomial transform.",
