    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_543a43f35b996ec02a178cf1542c291669fc9b4f4d6623c8670f9aefe0cc979a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The exact Li decomposition separates an explicit zeta sum from a binomial transform of the eta coefficients; the explicit sum has a rigorous leading (n/2) log n lower bound, so eventual Li positivity is reduced to proving that the eta transform is smaller than that scale. The sigma-eta identity motivates such cancellation through conjectured eta decay and alternation, but the required square-root-scale S2 estimate remains conjectural.",
