    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_b353c0d269c00abaf982dd9f14c1de91d88c84eed63ae1a4cd374eb6c3273082",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the source's completed Dirichlet and elliptic L-function constructions, differentiation separates universal conductor/gamma contributions from family-specific logarithmic-derivative prime-power sums. Rewriting the gamma side in common S0/S1/S3 coordinates yields explicit lower bounds with leading n log n growth, but eventual positivity still depends on conjectural cancellation of the arithmetic transforms; the analogous Dedekind construction stops earlier because convergence of its prime-ideal series is not justified.",
